- Summary:: The "pedagogy of poverty" describes teaching methods in urban schools that often limit student engagement and responsibility for learning. To improve education for at-risk students, schools need to involve the whole community and create a more interactive, meaningful learning environment. Good teaching happens when students are actively involved in planning, reflecting, and discussing important issues.
